WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.579
A shop recorded its daily profit in profits (a negative number is a loss). The owner must report

2
00:00:05.579 --> 00:00:12.143
one block of consecutive days whose length is at least minLen and at most maxLen. Return the largest

3
00:00:12.143 --> 00:00:17.385
total profit that a valid block can have. A block has to be reported even if every valid

4
00:00:17.385 --> 00:00:18.394
block loses money.

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:28.549
The days [5, -4, -1, 6] total 6, and so do the days [3, -2, 5]. No other

6
00:00:28.549 --> 00:00:28.960
block

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.321
of 2 to 4 days does better (for example [6, -3, 2] totals 5), so the answer is

8
00:00:37.321 --> 00:00:37.885
6.

9
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:46.174
Every valid block loses money. The best one is [-4, -2] with a total of -6; the whole

10
00:00:46.174 --> 00:00:47.965
record totals -13.

11
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.444
As the end moves right, the allowed starts slide right too, so the minimum prefix in the window

12
00:00:54.444 --> 00:00:57.623
can be kept in a deque that discards dominated candidates.

13
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.322
Build prefix totals. For each end from minLen to n, push the newly allowed start end - minLen

14
00:01:05.322 --> 00:01:10.825
after popping every back entry whose prefix is at least as large, pop the front while it is

15
00:01:10.825 --> 00:01:15.515
older than end - maxLen, and compare prefix[end] - prefix[front] with the best.

16
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:24.158
Each end wants the smallest prefix total among starts in [end - maxLen, end - minLen]. That window

17
00:01:24.158 --> 00:01:29.719
moves one step right per end, so this is a sliding-window minimum over the prefix array, which a

18
00:01:29.719 --> 00:01:31.878
monotonic deque solves in amortized

19
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.033
O(1). A start that is both later and no smaller than an earlier one will outlive it in

20
00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:43.239
the window and never lose to it, so the earlier one can be dropped. An index-based deque in

21
00:01:43.239 --> 00:01:45.357
